Two categories of startup warnings produced on every mangos.exe launch: missing C++ implementations for two DB-registered scripts, and `achievement_criteria_data` rows referencing classes/races that don't exist in Classic WoW.

## Missing script implementations

`achievement_pb_pilgrims_peril` and `achievement_pb_terokkar_turkey_time` were registered in the DB but had no code, causing loud warnings at load time. Added both to `achievement_scripts.cpp` using `HasItemWithIdEquipped` (CMaNGOS Classic API — not WotLK's `HasItemOrGemWithIdEquipped`):

```cpp
enum PilgrimItems
{
    ITEM_PILGRIMS_HAT    = 46723,
    ITEM_PILGRIMS_DRESS  = 44785,
    ITEM_PILGRIMS_ROBE   = 46824,
    ITEM_PILGRIMS_ATTIRE = 46800,
};

// Pilgrim's Peril: wearing costume body piece at enemy capital table
bool OnCheck(Player* source, ...) override
{
    return source->HasItemWithIdEquipped(ITEM_PILGRIMS_DRESS, 1)
        || source->HasItemWithIdEquipped(ITEM_PILGRIMS_ROBE, 1)
        || source->HasItemWithIdEquipped(ITEM_PILGRIMS_ATTIRE, 1);
}

// Terokkar Turkey Time: hat + body piece when killing Talon King Ikiss
bool OnCheck(Player* source, ...) override
{
    return source->HasItemWithIdEquipped(ITEM_PILGRIMS_HAT, 1)
        && (source->HasItemWithIdEquipped(ITEM_PILGRIMS_DRESS, 1)
            || source->HasItemWithIdEquipped(ITEM_PILGRIMS_ROBE, 1)
            || source->HasItemWithIdEquipped(ITEM_PILGRIMS_ATTIRE, 1));
}
```

## Invalid SQL entries

Removed 7 `achievement_criteria_data` rows (`criteria_id` 6302, 6313, 6319, 6320, 9124, 9143, 11163) that specified class 6 (Death Knight, WotLK-only) or races 10/11 (Blood Elf/Draenei, TBC+). The server was already ignoring and skipping these rows; removing them eliminates the warnings. Corresponding `DELETE` statements added to `sql/migrate/world_migrate.sql` for existing installs.

